Now byte_index = what was returned + oid_length. After get_expected_type_and_length returns, byte_index points to the OID value start, then we add oid_length, so byte_index = last_oid_byte = start_of_oid_value + oid_length.

This is bounded by last_byte1. So after reading the OID, byte_index <= last_byte1.

Then the call to validation_recursive uses `last_byte1 - byte_index` which is >= 0. No underflow.

